class.description:
The standard state node in a State Tree. Without child states, it acts as a leaf state; with child states, it acts as a compound state that activates one child at a time (starting with [member initial_state] if set, or choosing by [member NNSTBranchNodes.child_state_selection_rule]).
Override the lifecycle methods in a script (or connect to the corresponding signals on [NNSTTickedNodes]) to implement state behaviour:
[gdscript]
extends NNSTNode

func on_enter_condition() -> bool:
    return true

func on_enter_state() -> void:
    pass

func on_exit_state() -> void:
    pass

func on_tick(delta: float) -> void:
    pass
[/gdscript]
